      "word": "dune",
      "parts_of_speech": [
        "n"
      ],
      "definition": "沙丘；風堆積沙子形成的小山丘。",
      "explains": [
        {
          "guid": "c6a1c8c6-972f-5018-a5c5-16319004cec4",
          "en": "A dune is a hill of sand formed by the wind. Dunes are often found in deserts or near the sea."
        },
        {
          "guid": "0911ea0a-8280-5d4f-a6ca-c2856add5c60",
          "en": "This noun names a mound of sand. The wind can slowly change its shape or move it across the ground."
        },
        {
          "guid": "fbb737b5-e626-590e-856c-c68ba246fc7a",
          "en": "A dune is a natural pile of sand with sloping sides. Plants may grow on it and help hold the sand in place."
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "guid": "1e8fc5a1-79bb-58ff-b0de-8f2702affcda",
          "en": "The dune is near the beach.",
          "zh": "這座沙丘在海灘附近。"
        },
        {
          "guid": "719f1c2f-1c74-563c-8d69-faddf062508f",
          "en": "We walked up the sandy dune.",
          "zh": "我們走上了沙丘。"
        },
        {
          "guid": "1c9e2229-a58c-5dad-9e47-c9541ed287fc",
          "en": "The wind changed the shape of the dune.",
          "zh": "風吹改變了沙丘的形狀。"
        }
      ]
    },
